	Having a father from Montserrat, a British territory in the eastern Caribbean, and a mother from Alabama, he attended Murry Bergtraum High School in Manhattan, New York. In an interview with [a=Martha Stewart] he revealed that he got his nickname Q-Tip during his childhood because he was skinny and had big hair. 



	Described by fellow Quest member, Jarobi as the "Leader" on [a=A Tribe Called Quest]''s debut album, he is now considered as one of the leaders in the rap game. He helped pioneer a positive hip hop movement as part of the native tongues, and made it his duty to help and provide direction for some of the most talented artists over the years, such as [a=Busta Rhymes], [url=http://www.discogs.com/artist/Consequence+(2)]Consequence[/url], [a=Nas], [a=Mobb Deep], [a207029]. 



