	Patton started his career as pianist with the [a=Lloyd Price] touring band from 1954 to 1959, before moving to New York. Once there, he began to make the transition from piano to organ and recorded with [a=Lou Donaldson] for [l=Blue Note] from 1962 to 1964.

	In the mid 1980''s, Patton was rediscovered by a younger generation, particularly [a=John Zorn], who began using his sound on recordings, and Patton continued to release new recordings into the 1990''s, including two on the Japanese label [l=DIW Records].

