	Hugh Hopper was part of the so-called ''Canterbury scene''. Originally a member of The [a340389], he became roadie of [a152680] eventually replacing [a45646] in 1969, when the latter left, and stayed with the group until 1973, into what is considered the classic and most famous incarnation of the band. After leaving Soft Machine, he played mostly in the jazz / jazz rock vein with a vast number of different bands, many of them adopting a name with the word ''Soft'' as a reference to the success of Soft Machine.');



