	Lee graduated from Bard College with a focus on child psychology, literature, and dance choreography. During the mid-1960s, she adopted Fluxus-influenced multidisciplinarity and composed music for California-based sound poets Dr [a=David Hazelton], [a=Dick Higgins], and [a=Alison Knowles]. Hazelton was her first husband; the couple had a daughter, Naima Hazelton.



