	One of the most collected British jazz musicians of his era, Hayes began his professional career in his mid-teens, recording with [a272669] in [a2272354] (a group performing from 1957 to 1959), and leading a series of recordings for [l149875] and [l205]. Performed at the [l377602] in New York in 1961 and returned to the United States in 1962, 1964 and 1965. His health began to decline in the late-1960s and Hayes died from heart failure. A biography by [a1255801], "The Long Shadow of The Little Giant: The Life, Work and Legacy of Tubby Hayes" was published in 2015.');



