	Some of his current projects include [b][a=Harriet Tubman][/b] power-trio with bassist [a=Melvin Gibbs] and drummer [a=J.T. Lewis], in which Ross uses electronics and pan-tonality to create a multidimensional, interactive, sonic language in a "classic" R&B/rock configuration. Harriet Tubman released four albums, including a live CD on [a=John Zorn]''s [l=Avant] label in Japan. Brandon Ross also leads [b][a=For Living Lovers][/b], an all-acoustic duo with bass guitarist [a=Stomu Takeishi], which released their debut [r=6436588] album on [l=Sunnyside Communications] in 2014. He works with mezzo-soprano [a=Alicia Hall Moran] in [b]AiR[/b], leads a few experimental ensembles, such as [b]Brandon Ross''Pendulum[/b], [b]Phantom Station[/b] and [b](Yet)Another Plane[/b], and plays with guitarist [a=Doug Wieselman] and sound designer [a=Hardedge] as [b][a=DarkMatterHalo][/b] trio.



	As a performing and recording artist, Brandon Ross has been collaborating with numerous outstanding jazz musicians, including [a=Cassandra Wilson], [a=Jewel], [a=Lizz Wright], [a=Arto Lindsay], [a=John Lurie] and the [a=Lounge Lizards], [a=Butch Morris], [a=Bill Frisell], [a=Bill Laswell], [a=Me''Shell NdegéOcello], [a=Moreno Veloso], [a=Arrested Development], [a=Archie Shepp], [a=Muhal Richard Abrams], [a=Don Byron], [a=Gene Lake], [a=Marcus Rojas], [a=Geri Allen], and [a=Charles Burnham]. Ross was a member of various ensembles by [a=Henry Threadgill], [a=Oliver Lake], [a=Leroy Jenkins], [a=Myra Melford], [a=Marion Brown], [a=Rob Reddy], [a=Ron Miles], and [a=Wadada Leo Smith].');

