	Greene has been in the music business since 1963 as a guitarist, studio musician, recording artist, engineer and producer. He produced his first top 20 single in 1972 as a member of the recording group Swallow for Warner Brothers Records. His discography includes mixing New Kids on the Block''s 1988 ''Hangin'' Tough'' album, and Peter Wolf''s 2002 album ''Sleepless,'' featuring artists such as Keith Richards, Mick Jagger, and Steve Earl.



