	First coming to attention with singles released on [l=Mercury] Records in the mid-1950s, they went on to produce [a=Perry Como], [a=Elvis Presley], [a=Sam Cooke] and other artists for [l=RCA Victor], including the hit records "Twistin'' The Night Away", "Another Saturday Night", "The Lion Sleeps Tonight" by [a=Tokens], [a=The Isley Brothers]'' classic "Shout", and [a=Little Peggy March]''s "I Will Follow Him". 

