	Carlsson was active as a jazz musician from 1957 and studied at the Berklee College of Music in the USA in 1971. He played with, among others, [a31617], [a145272], [a252310], [a179055], [a64694], [a145263], [a251769], [a282438], and [a257115].



	Carlsson was influenced by modernists such as Art Blakey, Max Roach and Elvin Jones. His playing gave color to Sweden''s jazz elite in the latter half of the 20th century, in groups led by Arne Domnérus, Bengt Hallberg, Bo Hansson, Kjell Jansson, Åke Johansson, Red Mitchell, Lars Sjösten, Bobo Stenson and Eje Thelin.



