	Arlen''s common songwriting partner during the 1940s was [a=Johnny Mercer]. Together they wrote hit songs such as [i]Blues In The Night[/i] (1941), [i]One For My Baby (And One More For The Road)[/i] (1943) and [i]Ac-Cent-Tchu-Ate The Positive[/i] (1944). Although he was less active in later years, he successfully remained composing well into the 1970s. 



