	He is classically trained and was teached by [a567511]. In 1964, he and [a536592] met [a364124] in Nürnberg and founded together the "Contemporary Trio", a Jazz formation.

	They went to Munich and in 1969, him and Burchard founded together [a201948]. He played with the band until 1972, when they went on a tour through Portugal and Northern Africa. After that tour, Hofmann left the band.

	Edgar Hofmann has been a key player in the Bavarian Krautrock and fusion underground. He honed his craft as Jazz saxophonist in Munich underground Jazz clubs. After he left Embryo, he returned to the band frequently until the mid 1990''s. During that time, he also travelled all around the world to play music and he became a songwriter for theatre productions.');

	Burchard started his musical career as an organist in a rhythm & blues band in his teens, before moving to his preferred instrument - the vibraphone, later also taking up the drums.

	Born in Hof, he starts to play music with his schoolmate [a536592]. They move to Nürnberg in the 1960''s, where they meet saxophonist [a364117] and together they form the Jazz trio "Contemporary Trio". They move to Munich around 1967 and Burchard starts to play with Jazz pianist [a260727]. In 1968, the three musicians form a band together with [a338810], which in 1969 becomes [a201948]. Serfas and Meid leave the band in the early stage and Burchard stays leader of the band.

	Burchards concept for the band starts to be, to play in dynamic line-ups, when Embryo will end, more than 400 musicians will have played aside of Burchard.

	He records a first album with the band in 1970, many more follow the next years. Besides his role for Embryo, Burchard plays as guest musician with several other German bands as [a112963], [a699151] or [a708897]. Burchard also lets more world music influences into his music, which becomes unique in the mid 1970''s. In 1976, he is involved in the formation of the German independent label [l79234].

	In the 1990''s, he tours with the band all over the world, in 1996 his daughter [a2854290] joins the band at the age of 11. 

	His active music career ends in 2016, when he suffers a stroke.');

	From 1969, he played together with [a112963] and in 1973 for [a703253] as a bassist. A few months later, he joined [a201948] and stayed until the band divided in Embryo and Embryo''s Dissidenten.

