	Records cut at Dureco used a three or four character code/signature [b][w]wA[A]n[/b], where [i][w]w[/i] is one or two digits, marking the week of the year the record was cut, [i]A[A][/i] a single or double initial of the engineer who did the cut and [i]n[/i] the number of the cut. In these cases [l=Dureco Studio] can be credited with [i]Lacquer Cut At[/i] and the engineer with [i]Lacquer Cut By[/i], using the appropriate ANV for the initial(s). Grijpink signed his work with [i]C[/i], the initial of his Christian name. 



	Additionally, an etched [i]KG[/i] or [i]K.G.[/i] can sometimes be found, indicating that during the transfer to the lacquer, the sound of the recording was modified (in Grijpinks own words). In these cases an extra [i]Mastered By[/i] credit can be added with the appropriate ANV. When only [i]K.G.[/i] is present in the runout, both roles ([i]Lacquer Cut By[/i] and [i]Mastered By[/i]) can be used. With KG or K.G. an additional LCCN role [i]Mastered At[/i] [l=Dureco Studio] can be added.



