	He started his career in disc cutting as a trainee at [url=http://www.discogs.com/label/264470-Apple-Studios]Apple[/url] in 1968 and his signature can be found in the dead wax/runout grooves of many a rock, punk, post-punk, and new wave record pressed in the UK. Porky would often include cryptic/humorous messages in these etchings, e.g. "you''ll never work again" on the A-side of [a=The Fall] "[r=372019]" (1980). 



	Studios of his career include: [l=Apple Studios] (late 1960s), [l=Master Room] (early 1970s), [l=I.B.C. Studios]/[l=Portland Studios] (1974 to 1984), and [l=Porky''s Mastering] (since 1984). 

