	In 1981, Jean-Marc Foussat finished his debut album [m=858248], comprising experimental collages and studio recordings made in 1975–81 with VCS III synthesizer, piano, guitar, found vocals and field recordings. The album was self-released in March 1983 through his own imprint [l=Pyjama] and later considered by critics as one of the seminal works for the French avantgarde/musique concrete scene. An out-of-print cult album was reissued on bootleg CDr in 2014 by Keith Fullerton Whitman''s [l=Creel Pone] label.



	Foussat joined [a=Marteau Rouge] ensemble in 1991, with [a=Makoto Sato] on drums and [a=Jean-François Pauvros] on electric guitar. The trio collaborated with [a=Evan Parker]. From 2000 to 2013, Jean-Marc Foussat played in the free improvised group [a=Thrash The Flash] with guitarist [a=Marc Dufourd], vocalist [a=Lea Dufourd], [a=Damien Dufourd] on trumpet, and clarinet/flute player [a=Jérôme Bourdellon].



	In 2005, Foussat started [a=Aliquid] duo with saxophonist [a=Sylvain Guérineau] – they released three albums on [l=Leo Records], [l=Nashazphone] and [l=Fou Records], including a collaboration with [a=Joe McPhee]. Some of his recent projects include [a=Département d''Éducation Psychique] with [a=Dynamo Dreesen] and [a=Sven Rieger] (aka [a=SVN (2)], which debuted with a recording session in Paris in 2014 and released two ambient/drone LP albums, as well as an experimental house remix on [r8893408] 12" single.



	In 2016, Jean-Marc started [a=5599] duo with a French prodigy and adolescent improviser [a=Augustin Brousseloux] on electric guitar and alto saxophone. They released a debut [r=8819580] LP on Nashazphone label. Foussat participated in [i]MIA 2016[/i] ([i]7° Encontro de Música Improvisada de Atouguia da Baleia, Portugal[/i]) event in May 2016, as one of the 60+ members of [a=Ensemble MIA].



	Jean-Marc Foussat has been collaborating with [a=Jac Berrocal], [a=Roger Turner], [a=Raymond Boni] (as a member of [a=Raymond Boni Fortuna 21 Octet]), [a=Noël Akchoté], [a=Claude Parle], trumpeters [a=Jean-Luc Cappozzo], [a=Thomas Berghammer] and [a=Nicolas Souchal], trombonist [a=Matthias Mahler], vocalist [a=Marialuisa Capurso], drummers [a=Dirar Kalash] and [a=Paul Lovens], double bass player [a=Fred Marty] (in [b]MarsaFouty[/b] duo), turntablist [a=Hans Falb], violinist [a=Irene Kepl], [a=Samuel Blaser], [a=Emilie Lesbros], [a=Sophie Agnel], [a=Daunik Lazro] and numerous other musicians.



	As a gifted recording engineer, Jean-Marc Foussat worked extensively with [a=Joëlle Léandre] and [a=Joe McPhee], as well as [a=Bill Laswell] on [r820317]. He produced numerous live free-improvised recordings for such prominent independent labels, as [l=Incus], [l=Hat Hut Records], [l=Po Torch Records], [l=Rift], [l=RecRec Music], and [l=Celluloid].');

