	After graduation, he was hired for a Fort Collins, Colorado band named Kinesis with whom he recorded at Caribou Ranch.

	He moved back to Dallas for a couple of years before moving on to New York City, where he studied with Kenny Barron, Richie Beirach, and Fred Hersch.

	He played the Blue Note and Visiones, and the off-Broadway musical, "Little Shop of Horrors".

