	He graduated from New York State University at Potsdam with a B.S. and M.S. Degree in Percussion. Since then, he has been a performer (keyboards & percussion), arranger, producer, educator and composer of commercial jingles, albums and soundtracks. He has produced albums and arranged music for The Buddy Rich Band, The Glenn Miller Orchestra, Dan Truhitte (“Sound Of Music”), The Charlotte Symphony Orchestra and many more. Alan has performed with/accompanied acts as diverse as: Luciano Pavarotti, Johnny Cash, Bernadette Peters, Bobby Vinton, Clay Aiken, and others. Besides his professional duties, he has been Band Director with the Mecklenburg Area Catholic Schools since 1993.');



