	In 1951, Conkling became President of [l93330], where he initiated the [l174302] (which became [l55613]) and helped introduce long-playing (LP) records.  He also helped organize and served as President of the Record Industry Association of America ([l255302]).



	In 1957, he joined four other record executives to found the [l409941], which sponsors the Grammy awards. Conkling served as the group’s founding Chairman and produced the first Grammy awards shows. In 1995, the Grammy’s [l697051] Division honored him with a lifetime achievement award and staged a fund-raising dinner for Alzheimer’s research.



