	Runouts contain identifying symbols that can be used to determine a month/year of cutting based on the following:



	(Approx 1953-1955)

	"DH" with no "T" or accompanying number - [r7886567], [r12543915]



	(Approx. 1955-1960)

	T xx - T followed by 1-2 digit number, up to about T78. Numbers are in chronological order, see examples below



	(Approx 1960-1966)

	2-3 digit number without "T" marking, 73 up to about 152. Numbers are in chronological order, see examples below



	Numbering/date examples (assuming release 1-2 months after production, compare with Billboard release dates):

	T#2/T#3 - [r17192542] (VRS-8511) - 1956

	3T - [r15703507] - "Recorded Fall 1955"

	T26 - [r34614193] (TLP 1010) - 11-21-57 etch

	T42 - (MF 307) - 7-11-58/7-22-58, (MP 530) - 7-18-58, (EKL-154) - 7-17-58

	T43 - [r19686619} (MF 308) - 8-9-58 etch

	T66 - [r8292667] (TSP2) - 9-2-59 etch

	T67 - [r13421210] (TLP 1036) - 9-22-59 etch

	T69 - TLP 1025, 10-30-59 etch



	96 (no "T") - [r3017411] (TLP 1008 repress) - 11-30-60 etch

	119 (no "T") - [r5591351] (Nyland 338) - 9-7-62 etch, [r4125781] (MF 389) - 11-30-62 etch



	Miscellaneous symbols:

	ORIG - David was the both recording and mastering engineer for the release (may appear on one side of the LP if he did not record the entire album). Examples - [r4628895]. [r1669218]

	AX/BX or AN/BN - new lacquer cut (late 1950s to early 1960s). Example - [r23848238]



	ORT1 through ORT5 - Ortofon cutting equipment (1966-1968)

	ANM - Capps ANM cutting equipment (1967- mid 1970s)

	MP - (1967- mid 1980s)











