	Quote from Blockbusters member [a266392]: "The Boots Brown dates were for movies but then RCA released them as singles. I don’t know why - maybe to make a double profit or to feed the pipeline for its new 45-rpm format. But you have to remember, at the time it wasn''t cool to play that kind of music if you played jazz. That''s why Shorty came up with a fake name. I don’t know why he chose Boots Brown or what it meant. I know we didn''t want our names on the records. We were too embarrassed."');

