	The orchestra came into existence as a rehearsal band around 1965.The debut appearance of the orchestra, at the [l=Village Vanguard] jazzclub, was Monday February 7, 1966.  That is where the legendary Monday Night Concert Series started. The band performed ca 12 years in its original incarnation and did world wide tours.



	In 1978 Thad Jones moved to Copenhagen (Denmark) and led the Danish Radio Big Band for several years. The Thad Jones/Mel Lewis band was continued by Mel Lewis alone, then as [a=The Mel Lewis Jazz Orchestra]. 



	After the death of Mel Lewis in 1990, the orchestra was continued under the name [a=The Vanguard Jazz Orchestra]. Trombonist John Mosca is responsible for the band at the moment. 



	Almost 60 years after the inception, The Monday Night sessions at the [l=Village Vanguard] are still happening.');



