	Rael was a saxophone player, with his own band in the Army during WWII when he discovered Patti Page (then Clara Ann Fowler from Tulsa Oklahoma) and helped her become one of the most respected and beloved singers of the 1950''s 60''s and beyond, selling more record than any female artist of that era.



