	"Orville was born in Baltimore, Maryland, in 1940.  He is part of a large, loving, musical family which also includes his first cousins, jazz pianist, Ronnie Matthews and Victor Myrick, professor of Music at the Peabody Institute in Baltimore.  He first studied bass, for four years, with Frederick Zimmerman, second bassist with the New York Philharmonic.  He has also studied with Paul Chambers, Ron Carter, Jimmy Garrison, and Doug Watkins.  Orville has played with a host of well-known musicians, including Chris Anderson, Rahn Burton, Charles Davis, Tex Allen, Ronnie Matthews, Earl Clark, and Jeff Hittman.  Seldom without a group of his own, whether duo, trio, quartet or quintet, Orville has played at clubs and restaurants all over the Eastern Seaboard and in Europe.  He appears on several recordings, among them, the classic "It is Revealed," with Clifford Jordan and Don Cherry."



