	Tim went to the Berklee College of Music in Boston and studied Jazz theory and majored in Music Production and Engineering. After finishing the program at Berklee he started work at Clinton Recording Studios in Hells Kitchen - New York City.



	Unfortunately, Clinton Studios were closed for good in 2010 and have since been demolished. It was then that Tim and his fellow house engineer at Clinton for many years, Bryan Smith, decided to pool there resources and open a new studio in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. There idea was to put together a space that could be affordable to work out of for small projects, but still achieve the highest quality and standards they and there clients had been accustomed to at Clinton. On January 1st 20011 Brooklyn Aloha Recording Studio was born.



	Over the years Tim has recorded a wide range of music from Jazz and Orchestral to Rock, Pop, Movie Scores and Audio Books. He has also had the chance to work with some of the biggest names in the music world.



