	Studied music theory and composition at University of Texas. Played Hammond and piano local restaurants, staff organist for Texas State Network, conducted informal 10 pc orchestra for campus social events.  Moved to NYC in 1942, playing keyboard at several popular nightspots.  Formed Milt Page Trio.  Appointed staff organist at Roxy Theater in 1947.  Also played Hammond for radio and TV shows.  Appointed staff organist at Radio City in 1948 and continued background work for radio and TV.  Returned to Texas in 1949 and received Doctorate of Music from Southern College of Fine Arts, Houston. Later became an arranger and editor for the Ethel Smith Music Corporation, which published instruction books and arrangements for Hammond organs. PAGE ONE is part of a teaching lesson entitled "Duet Yourself No 1" with the student playing the arrangements along with tracks on the record.   Milton Page also toured the US presenting Teacher''s Workshops and playing concerts on Hammond Organs.  ');

