	As a pit drummer on Broadway, Harris opened 30 shows in 14 years, including “On the Town,” by [a=Leonard Bernstein], “Call Me Mister,” and the Broadway musical that propelled [a=Carol Channing] to fame, “Gentlemen Prefer Blondes.”



