	He studied at the Regino Boti School in Guantánamo with Nelson Betancourt. He then joined the National Art School of Havana where he will hold the Golden Diploma of Music, then the Higher Institute of Art in Psychology and Pedagogy of Cuban Percussion Education which he will later become the percussion teacher. In 1997 he obtained the Gold Diploma of Music Teacher and also won the first prize in the symphonic duos and percussion competition in Havana.



	After winning several awards in Havana, his native country, and after an internship in 1998 with [a=Wynton Marsalis], he participated as a percussionist of Cuban flutist group [a=Orlando "Maraca" Valle] Y Otra Visión, at various Festivals: in Havana, Vitoria (Spain), Switzerland, Los Angeles, New York, San Francisco.

	 

	He was professor of percussion at the Higher Institute of the Arts in Cuba, until March-July 2002 where he came on tour in France with Las Hermanas Faez and Casa de la Trova.

