	Pye record cuts by him can be identified by △S, ♢S, ✳S (1964 - 1968) and △W and ♢W (1968 - 1974). 
	The symbols identify the cutting suites:
	The diamond: until 1974 identifying the Westrex/Scully lathe and from 1974 onwards identifying the Neumann SX74 lathe.
	The triangle: until 1968 identifying the Westrex/Scully lathe and from 1968 onwards identifying the Neumann SX68 lathe.
	The star: identifying the Westrex/Scully mono lathe, operative until ca. 1974.
	Please use 
	Lacquer Cut At - Pye Studios, and 
	Lacquer Cut By - Derek Sticklen + ANV S or ANV W (without symbol).

	Do not confuse ♢S and ♢W with masterings from Deutsche Grammophon (usually coming with a ℗ + year, and/or a letter + number, e.g. L8).

