	Records cut at Dureco used a three or four character code/signature [b][w]wA[A]n[/b], where [i][w]w[/i] is one or two digits, marking the week of the year the record was cut, [i]A[A][/i] a single or double initial of the engineer who did the cut and [i]n[/i] the number of the cut. In these cases the studio can be credited with [i]Lacquer Cut At[/i] and the engineer with [i]Lacquer Cut By[/i], using the appropriate ANV for the initial(s). Kooij had a specific way of signing his work, using the initial [i]A[/i] on one side and [i]K[/i] on the other, but also used initial [i]A[/i] or initial [i]K[/i] on both sides. Please use each letter as a separate ANV.');

